qualityObjective.en:
Verify that installed equipment and systems actually perform their intended operational functions, not merely that they have been installed.
Examples:
door closes and latches;
valve operates;
damper opens/closes;
HVAC responds to command;
drain actually drains;
emergency light operates;
alarm interface triggers expected physical response.

This is where separate systems are tested together.
Verify that interacting systems operate correctly as an integrated facility under defined scenarios.
Examples:
fire alarm → damper → door release → emergency system;
emergency power → emergency lighting;
BAS → HVAC equipment;
equipment shutdown/interlock sequences.
